  76     // mstatus: enable FS / VS so the following FPR / V abstract writes are
  77     // accepted (FS or VS == Off disables the extension and the hart NACKs
  78     // the writes). The drained state.mstatus may legitimately carry FS or
  79     // VS at Off (e.g. an OS context-switched the regs away before the
  80     // trigger fired) -- gating the write on the drained field skips the
  81     // enable and silently NACKs every subsequent FPR / V-CSR write. Always
  82     // write mstatus when either extension is in scope; force-OR Initial
  83     // when the drained field is Off. This enable is local to the vsim
  84     // phase; the state.mstatus written to the handoff file is left
